.TH DARQOS-BACKUP 8 2026-11-03 DarqOS "DarqOS System Manager's Manual"
.SH NAME
darqos-backup \- back up DarqOS's run directory
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B /darq/bin/darqos-backup
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B darqos-backup
takes a snapshot of DarqOS's run directory, keeps the last few, and
copies them to the backup destination, if there's one.
It's run daily, as root, by
.IR darqos-backup.timer ,
and at the next boot after a run that was missed.
.PP
A snapshot is a directory in
.BR $SNAPSHOTS ,
named by its time
.RI ( YYYYMMDD-HHMMSS ):
each database copied with SQLite's online backup
.RB ( sqlite3 " .backup" ),
so a running DarqOS can go on writing to it, and the other files as
they are, without the databases' write-ahead logs.
Then all but the last
.B $KEEP
are removed, and, if
.B $BACKUP_DEST
is set, they're copied there with
.BR "rsync \-a \-\-delete" .
.PP
To restore one, stop DarqOS, and copy its files into the run
directory, owned by
.BR darq .
.SH CONFIGURATION
.I /etc/darqos/backup.conf
is read as shell assignments.
.BR install (8)
creates it, and leaves it alone after.
.TP
.B BACKUP_DEST
Where snapshots are copied: a directory, or
.IB host : directory
over SSH, with root's key.
Empty, the default, they're only kept locally.
.TP
.B KEEP
How many snapshots to keep.
Default: 7.
.TP
.B SNAPSHOTS
Where they're kept.
Default:
.IR /var/backups/darqos .
.TP
.B RUN_DIR
What's backed up.
Default:
.IR /darq/run .
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B DARQOS_BACKUP_CONF
The configuration file, if not
.IR /etc/darqos/backup.conf .
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /var/backups/darqos
The snapshots, mode 0700.
.TP
.I /darq/kernel/darqos-backup.service
.TQ
.I /darq/kernel/darqos-backup.timer
Its
.BR systemd (1)
units, installed into
.IR /etc/systemd/system .
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 if the snapshot was taken and copied; otherwise non-zero, with the
partial snapshot removed at the next run.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR install (8),
.BR rsync (1),
.BR sqlite3 (1)
